# Safe-chain Policy

Never use `--safe-chain-skip-minimum-package-age` when running pip, poetry, or any Python package installer. If a package is blocked by safe-chain's minimum age check, either:

1. Pin to an older version that passes the check
2. Wait for the package to age past the threshold
3. Ask the user before proceeding

This protects against supply-chain attacks via newly published malicious packages.
